### Do not cache an empty materialized shell image

**Severity:** `medium`

The extraction path can return a non-null `ImageIconSource` whose `ImageSource` is still null after bitmap materialization fails. Because later cache code treats that as a successful icon, the blank source can be cached and reused instead of falling back. Convert empty materialized images to the existing Shell fallback before completing the load.

```suggestion
                if (extractionResult.TakeSoftwareBitmap() is { } softwareBitmap)
                {
                    result = await CreateSoftwareBitmapIconSourceAsync(softwareBitmap, diagnostics).ConfigureAwait(false);
                    if (result is ImageIconSource { ImageSource: null })
                    {
                        result = await GetShellItemFallbackSourceAsync(diagnostics).ConfigureAwait(false);
                    }
                }
                else if (extractionResult.BitmapStream is { } bitmapStream)
                {
                    result = await CreateImageIconSourceAsync(bitmapStream, scaledSize, diagnostics).ConfigureAwait(false);
                    if (result is ImageIconSource { ImageSource: null })
                    {
                        result = await GetShellItemFallbackSourceAsync(diagnostics).ConfigureAwait(false);
                    }
                }
```

### Remove the misleading extraction-avoidance percentage

**Severity:** `low`

A progressive Shell request can do both provisional and exact extraction, so extraction count is not bounded by request count. Keep the concrete counters and route breakdown instead of deriving a misleading percentage from mismatched units.

```suggestion
        builder.AppendLine("    Extraction routes");
        AppendEnumCounts<ShellIconIdentityKind>(builder, _shellIconExtractionKinds, "      ");
        builder.AppendLine("    Direct system image-list extraction");
```
